From c79b6f6541583b148354b731691dc92caeac6adb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shandongtlb <40312509+shandongtlb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:20:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wlan: restore monitor WEXT and discard stale host queues on
 retune
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port sam monitor WEXT name/mode/frequency/range handlers to peach, using
confirmed channel reads and the existing channel lock. Accept idempotent
20 MHz confirmation; keep actual retuning on nl80211 to avoid waiting for
firmware under RTNL.

Drain RX-only host traffic to rejection instead of retaining it. Detach
and reset qdisc under a short RTNL trylock before helper/channel changes,
block admission across the transition, and resume the empty queue on all
exits. Preserve the running helper on same-channel confirmation and retain
capacity-based stop/wake flow control.

This commit preserves all 11 files from the v7 build snapshot byte for
byte. The unified sun perf build and 11 ASan/UBSan host checks passed;
five affected host checks also passed at closeout. Installed v7 module
identities matched, WEXT Probe passed 30/30 in three rounds, and 40/80 MHz
queue tests showed no old packets submitted after returning to 20 MHz.
A 128-frame burst reached peak 62 and drained fully. Device evidence is
recorded separately; SSR and long-running stress remain unvalidated.

Primary reference: sam/补丁/0001-wlan-native-monitor-injection.patch.
Historical oplus qca_inject/0011 and 0012 WEXT patches are reference only.
